course: dictionary
lesson: 6279
title: Monsieur, the polite word for sir
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Monsieur is a French word. It means "Mr" or "sir", and you use it to speak politely to a man. «Bonjour, monsieur!» means "Good morning, sir!"
explain: When you see M. before a name, as in M. Dupont, it is short for monsieur. It means Mr Dupont. The word sounds like "muh-SYUR" to an English ear.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «Bonjour» means hello, so «Bonjour, monsieur!» is a greeting to a man. Ask yourself what the word is doing in the sentence, then check your meaning by swapping it in.
explain: In some English stories, monsieur is used as a joke to make a man sound French. That is a joke in English, not the real French meaning, so always check which language the text is in.
fact: Monsieur is a French word, not an English one.
fact: «Monsieur» means "Mr" or "sir".
fact: The plural of monsieur is messieurs, as in «Mesdames et messieurs», which means ladies and gentlemen.
fact: In France it is polite to say monsieur or madame when you greet a shopkeeper.
fact: «Croque-monsieur» is a toasted ham and cheese sandwich; croquer means to crunch.
exercise: «Bonjour, monsieur!» What does monsieur mean here? | Goodbye | A type of bread | *Sir, or Mr
exercise: What is the plural of monsieur? | *messieurs | monsieurs | madame | mademoiselles
exercise: How can you politely get a waiter's attention in France? | Throw a coin on the table | Click your fingers and shout Garçon! | Shout "Hey, you!" across the room | *Catch his eye, smile and say S'il vous plaît, monsieur!
test: Which French word means "Mr" or "sir"? | madame | mademoiselle | garçon | *monsieur
test: In «M. Dupont», what does M. stand for? | Madame | Maman | Mademoiselle | *Monsieur
exam: Which greeting is correct and polite to say to a man in French? | *Bonjour, monsieur! | Bonjour, garçon! | Merci, mademoiselle! | Au revoir, madame!
